From c8bde7c4cd19327d3630182f9b9d451edfeef974 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:17:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/60] fix-data-3: places (D-41, D-42, V-45, Town and Country,
 old location links) and department names (UX-32); norm-12

- geo.js: one 'St.' spelling for US (and Canadian 'St') towns; 'New York State', 'Washington State' and
  'Washington, DC' for state-only places; Cajamar, six other Brazilian towns and Luxembourg City in the
  gazetteer; Amazon's 'City, State, CCC' is one place; 'Town and Country' is one place, also when stored split.
- families.js departmentDisplayName + upgrade.js displayDepartments: NVIDIA's inverted names and 'Intern', and
  Amazon's '--' names, read naturally at read time; the board's name stays as departmentPosted.
- app.js: search matches departmentPosted; an old link's location or department value resolves to the
  board's current label (resolveOldFilterKeys).
- roles.js: NVIDIA's verification department still reads as chip design under its new name.
- NORMALIZER_VERSION norm-12; golden re-baselined with the tooling: 0 of 300 hashes changed.
- docs/process/patches/fix-data-3-shared-posted-places.diff: payLocations' postedPlaces, as juice.js (for the lead).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
(cherry picked from commit e0f828a5668d3a9c91ec218b1b461475b8ce67f4)
